{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so of a truth: but how should man be just with God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he will contend with him, he cannot answer him one of a thousand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise in heart, and mighty in strength: who hath hardened ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against him, and hath prospered?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who removeth the mountains, and they know not: who overturneth them in his anger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who shaketh the earth out of her place, and its pillars tremble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who commandeth the sun, and it riseth not; and sealeth up the stars.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who alone spreadeth out the heavens, and treadeth upon the waves of the sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who maketh Arcturus, Orion, and Pleiades, and the chambers of the south.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who doeth great things past finding out; yes, and wonders without number.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, he goeth by me, and I see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not: he passeth on also, but I perceive him not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he taketh away, who can hinder him? who will say to him, What doest thou?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God will not withdraw his anger, the proud helpers do stoop under him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much less shall I answer him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " choose out my words ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to reason",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom, though I were righteous, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would I not answer, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I would make supplication to my judge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I had called, and he had answered me; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I would not believe that he had hearkened to my voice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he breaketh me with a tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I speak",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of strength, lo, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strong: and if of judgment, who shall set me a time ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to plead",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I justify myself, my own mouth will condemn me: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if I say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perfect, that also will prove me perverse.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perfect, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would I not know my soul: I would despise my life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", therefore I said ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he destroyeth the perfect and the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the scourge shall slay suddenly, he will laugh at the trial of the innocent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The earth is given into the hand of the wicked: he covereth the faces of its judges; if not, where, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now my days are swifter than a post: they flee away, they see no good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are passed away as the swift ships: as the eagle ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hasteth to the prey.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I say, I will forget my complaint, I will leave off my heaviness, and comfort ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "myself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am afraid of all my sorrows, I know that thou wilt not hold me innocent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I am wicked, why then do I labor in vain?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I wash myself with snow water, and make my hands never so clean;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet wilt thou plunge me in the ditch, and my own clothes shall abhor me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a man, as I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I should answer him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " we should come together in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither is there any judge between us, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " might lay his hand upon us both.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him take away his rod from me, and let not his fear terrify me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.9.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would I speak, and not fear him; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not so with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
